.TH kb 1  "kb 0.5.0" 
.SH NAME
kb \- Cross\-platform CLI for managing the knowledge\-base ecosystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkb\fR [\fB\-\-kb\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Cross\-platform CLI for managing the knowledge\-base ecosystem
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-kb\-root\fR \fI<KB_ROOT>\fR
Override knowledge\-base root discovery
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output machine\-readable JSON
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Quiet output — suppress informational messages
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
kb\-init(1)
One\-time setup on a new machine
.TP
kb\-link(1)
Wire a project repository to the knowledge\-base
.TP
kb\-unlink(1)
Remove symlinks for a project (keeps memory)
.TP
kb\-archive(1)
Move a project\*(Aqs memory to archive/ (or restore it with \-\-restore)
.TP
kb\-open(1)
Open a project\*(Aqs KB directory (or the knowledge\-base root) in your editor or file manager
.TP
kb\-status(1)
Overview of the knowledge\-base on this machine
.TP
kb\-doctor(1)
Health check across the knowledge\-base
.TP
kb\-projects(1)
List all projects in the knowledge\-base
.TP
kb\-clone\-refs(1)
Clone missing reference repos from ref/README.md
.TP
kb\-sync(1)
Sync with remote: git pull \-\-rebase + re\-link
.TP
kb\-global\-sync(1)
Bidirectional sync of the whole KB: pull if safe, then push everything
.TP
kb\-pull(1)
Pull knowledge\-base updates (fast\-forward only)
.TP
kb\-push(1)
Push changes for specific projects to remote
.TP
kb\-export(1)
Export project memory to a portable tarball
.TP
kb\-import(1)
Import project memory from a tarball
.TP
kb\-completions(1)
Generate shell completions
.TP
kb\-man(1)
Generate man page
.TP
kb\-work(1)
Start working on a project (sync + link + track)
.TP
kb\-done(1)
Finish working: commit + push tracked projects
.TP
kb\-search(1)
Search memory files across the knowledge\-base
.TP
kb\-log(1)
Show recent knowledge\-base history from git
.TP
kb\-rules(1)
Ensure the personal kb\-rules.md map for a project
.TP
kb\-subscribe(1)
Subscribe this device to a project\*(Aqs memory (selective sync)
.TP
kb\-unsubscribe(1)
Stop receiving a project\*(Aqs memory on this device
.TP
kb\-config(1)
Inspect and edit machine\-local configuration
.TP
kb\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Run `kb <command> \-\-help` for more information on a command.
.SH VERSION
v0.5.0
